## What Are Recalls and Why They Matter?

A car recall occurs when a manufacturer discovers a defect in a vehicle that could pose a safety risk. These defects can range from malfunctioning brakes to faulty airbags.

When cars are recalled, the manufacturer is required to notify owners and fix the problem - usually free of charge. From there, it’s the customer’s decision whether or not they take care of the recall.

Ignoring a recall notice could mean driving with a hidden danger that could put you and your passengers at risk.

For instance, Takata’s airbag recall, which has now been linked to 28 deaths in the U.S., is a clear reminder of why it’s important not to overlook safety notices. _Quickly_ taking action on a recall, even for what seems like a small issue, can prevent serious accidents and keep everyone safer on the road.

## Toyota Recalled Cars in 2024

In 2024, [Toyota issued recalls](/manufacturers/toyota) for several of its models. Some of these issues may seem minor, but others could require immediate attention to avoid accidents or long-term damage to your vehicle.

If you own one of the following models, it’d be wise to check if your car is impacted:

## 1. Toyota Camry: Airbag System Malfunctions

A. Models Affected

- Avalon, Avalon Hybrid (2020-2021)

- Camry, Camry Hybrid (2020-2022)

- Corolla (2020-2021)

- Highlander, Highlander Hybrid (2020-2021)

- RAV4, RAV4 Hybrid (2020-2021)

- Sienna Hybrid (2021)

B. Airbag Issues

At the very end of 2023 and the beginning of 2024, a Toyota recall includes nearly [1 million vehicles](https://thehill.com/homenews/4370741-toyota-recalls-1-million-vehicles-over-possible-airbag-failure/), the Toyota Camry being among them.

Reports suggest that the airbags may not deploy properly in the event of a collision, which can significantly increase the risk of injury or even death in the event of a crash. Toyota is urging Camry owners to schedule a repair as soon as possible to prevent this dangerous malfunction from affecting their safety.

## 2. Toyota Grand Highlander: Passenger Side Airbag

A. Models Affected

- 2024 Toyota Grand Highlander

- 2024 Lexus TX

B. Passenger Airbag Problems

In June 2024, Toyota issued a recall involving approximately 145,000 vehicles, including the 2024 Toyota Grand Highlander and Lexus TX models. Owners of affected vehicles were notified in August 2024​.

The issue centers around the passenger-side curtain airbags, which may not deploy properly during certain crashes if the driver’s or passenger’s windows are rolled down. This failure to meet federal safety standards could increase the risk of injury to passengers in specific accident scenarios.

## 3. Toyota Tundra and Sequoia: Transmission Issue

A. Models Affected

- 2022-2024 Toyota Tundra

- 2022-2024 Toyota Tundra Hybrid

- 2023-2024 Toyota Sequoia

- 2022-2024 Lexus LX 600

B. Transmission Problems

In February 2024, Toyota recalled approximately 280,000 vehicles, including Tundra, Sequoia, and Lexus LX 600 models. The recall was issued due to a defect in the transmission system that prevents the vehicle from fully disengaging power when shifted to neutral - increasing the risk of a low-speed crash.

Toyota has taken immediate action to remedy the situation by offering a free software update to affected vehicle owners.

## 4. Toyota Multi-Model Recall: Load Carrying Capacity Label Error

A. Models Affected

- 2023 Toyota GR Supra

- 2024 Toyota 4Runner

- 2024 Toyota Corolla Cross Hybrid

- 2024 Toyota Grand Highlander Hybrid

- And more…

B. Load Carrying Capacity Label Error

In July 2024, Toyota issued a recall impacting over [22 different models](https://www.abc3340.com/news/nation-world/toyota-recall-recalls-recalled-more-than-22-models-4runner-bz4x-corolla-cross-hybrid-cincinnati-consumer-alerts-danger-dangerous-products-crown-gr-supra-gr86-grand-highlander-hybrid-land-cruiser-prius-prime-sequoia-tacoma-tundra-venza-latest-model-top) due to a labeling issue related to the load-carrying capacity of these vehicles. The error involves an incorrect maximum capacity weight displayed on the modification labels, which could result in vehicle overloading.

Toyota has responded by mailing updated labels to affected vehicle owners at no cost. Owners are encouraged to apply the new label to their vehicles or visit a dealership to have it done.

## 5. Toyota Engine Stall Recall: Over 100,000 Vehicles Affected

A. Models Affected

- 2022-2023 Toyota Tundra

- 2022-2023 Toyota Tundra Hybrid

B. Engine Stall Problems

In June 2024, Toyota recalled over 100,000 vehicles in the U.S. due to a risk of engine stalling. The recall affects the 2022-2023 Toyota Tundra and Tundra Hybrid models, which may experience a loss of engine power due to a software issue in the engine control unit. This malfunction can cause the vehicle to unexpectedly stall while driving, increasing the risk of a crash.

Toyota is providing free software updates to resolve the issue. Affected vehicle owners were notified in June 2024, and Toyota dealerships are offering the necessary fixes to ensure engine reliability and prevent stalling

## What to Do if Your Vehicle is Recalled?

## How to Check

The good news is that it’s easy to find out if your Toyota is part of the recall. Toyota owners can visit the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (NHTSA) website and enter their Vehicle Identification Number (VIN). You can also contact your Toyota dealer directly to check your car’s recall status.

## Steps to Take

If your Toyota is recalled, the manufacturer is required to repair the issue at no cost to you. Once you’ve confirmed your vehicle is affected, here’s what to do next:

- **Schedule a Service Appointment**: Contact your local Toyota dealership to set up a repair appointment.

- **Understand the Timeline**: Some recalls require immediate attention, while others may have a longer time frame for repairs.

- **Get the Repairs Done**: Depending on the issue, repairs may take anywhere from a few hours to a couple of days.

## Your Rights as a California Toyota Owner

Under [lemon law in CA](/info/how-it-works), if your vehicle has persistent issues that aren’t resolved after a reasonable number of repair attempts, you could be entitled to compensation. A skilled lemon law attorney in CA can help protect consumers by requiring manufacturers to replace or refund vehicles that have serious defects.

Compensation may include:

- A **refund** of your purchase price

- A **replacement vehicle** of similar value

- Repair cost reimbursement

If your Toyota has been in for repairs multiple times and the problem persists, it’s important to know your rights under the lemon law in CA regulations.

